    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 50\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 4847-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to prohibit-\n      ing individuals in certain positions from taking any position with\n      a business or entity doing business with an industrial development\n      authority\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  create  new  prohibitions on the types of financial\ninterests that employees, board members, and contractors  of  Industrial\nDevelopment Authorities (IDAs) may hold.\n \n  This  bill is very similar to legislation I vetoed last year. It would\nimpose new restrictions on certain employees, members,  and  contractors\nof  IDAs,  prohibiting  them  from  holding interests that are otherwise\nlawfully permitted by the General Municipal  Law.  The  State's  General\nMunicipal Law already prohibits employees and board members of IDAs from\nholding  interests  in  any  contract  with their respective IDAs if the\nindividual has the power  to  negotiate  or  authorize  such  contracts,\nsubject   to   certain   exceptions.   The  purpose  of  these  existing\nrestrictions is to protect the integrity  of  local  government  and  to\nidentify and mitigate conflicts of interest.\n \n  I  remain  committed  to working to restore trust in government, and I\nsupport strengthening ethics safeguards in  local  government.  However,\nthe  creation  of  a new standard that conflicts with existing standards\nelsewhere in the General Municipal Law generates the risk  of  confusion\nand  arbitrary  application.  Additionally, these new restrictions could\npose operational challenges for local IDAs as it limits  their  pool  of\navailable employees and partners.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 50,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2023
   }
